---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Byline from '../components/Byline.astro';
import PublicationDate from '../components/PublicationDate.astro';
import { getPublishedPieces } from '../lib/lab';
import { authorRegistry, kindLabels } from '../lib/lab-schema';
import '../styles/knowledge.css';
const pieces = await getPublishedPieces();
---
<SiteLayout title="Inside Fidret — Purpose, practice and work" description="How Fidret connects its purpose, developing Physical AI practice and public work. Explore the company charter, experiments and Lab." canonical="https://fidret.com/project/">
  <main id="main" class="knowledge-page project-page">
    <header class="knowledge-hero shell">
      <p class="section-context">Inside Fidret</p>
      <h1>A company taking shape.</h1>
      <div class="knowledge-hero-copy"><p class="knowledge-lead">Expertise earns trust through the work, and through the judgment behind it.</p><p>Fidret is being built around that idea. Here is how the purpose, the first practice and the work connect.</p></div>
    </header>

    <section class="project-map-section inverse" aria-labelledby="map-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="knowledge-section-heading"><h2 id="map-title">One purpose.<br />Room to develop.</h2><p>Fidret is the company. Physical AI is its first practice. Experiments and writing help make the thinking inspectable.</p></div>
        <div class="project-map">
          <div class="project-map-purpose"><p class="project-map-label">The purpose</p><h3>Trust earned.</h3><p>Sound judgment, useful work and reliable delivery.</p><a class="text-link" href="/charter/">Read the company charter</a></div>
          <div class="project-map-practice"><p class="project-map-label">The first practice</p><h3>Physical AI</h3><p>Systems that observe physical environments and support decisions or actions within them.</p><span class="project-map-state">In development</span></div>
          <div class="project-map-work"><p class="project-map-label">The work we share</p><h3>Experiments &amp; Lab</h3><p>Bounded software explorations, their methods and limits, and technical writing with explicit bylines.</p><a class="text-link" href="/lab/">Explore the Lab</a></div>
        </div>
        <p class="project-map-note">Purpose sets the direction. Practice frames the questions. Evidence determines what the work can support.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="knowledge-split shell project-foundation" aria-labelledby="foundation-title">
      <div><h2 id="foundation-title">A foundation<br />others can follow.</h2><p>Useful work should remain understandable when someone else picks it up.</p></div>
      <div class="knowledge-prose"><p>Our project foundation records purpose, decisions, task ownership and verification alongside implementation. The intent is to make the reasoning recoverable, rather than leave it in a conversation.</p><p>Agents can assist with the work. Named people remain responsible for its scope, acceptance and consequences. A passing check supports a specific technical claim; it does not establish every promise a company makes.</p><a class="text-link" href="/approach/">How we intend to earn trust</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="knowledge-work shell" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="knowledge-section-heading"><h2 id="work-title">Start with a question<br />you can inspect.</h2><p>The current exploration is synthetic software. It helps explain a policy without implying a validated physical system.</p></div>
      <a class="knowledge-feature" href="/explorations/signal-freshness/">
        <div><p class="knowledge-feature-kind">Software exploration</p><h3>When is a signal<br />too old?</h3></div>
        <div><p>Follow a reading through silence, delay and recovery. See why arrival time alone cannot establish freshness.</p><span class="knowledge-feature-action">Open the walkthrough</span></div>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="knowledge-publications shell" aria-labelledby="publications-title">
      <div class="knowledge-section-heading"><h2 id="publications-title">From the Lab</h2><p>Published pieces keep the question, method, takeaways and limits together.</p></div>
      {pieces.length > 0 ? <div class="knowledge-piece-list">{pieces.map(piece => <article class="knowledge-piece"><div class="knowledge-piece-meta"><span>{kindLabels[piece.data.kind]}</span><PublicationDate value={piece.data.published} /></div><div><h3><a href={`/lab/${piece.data.slug}/`}>{piece.data.title}</a></h3><p>{piece.data.summary}</p><p class="knowledge-piece-credit">By <Byline authors={piece.data.authors} /></p></div></article>)}</div> : <div class="knowledge-empty"><h3>The written work is still ahead.</h3><p>For now, the signal-freshness walkthrough offers one concrete question to explore. Written pieces will appear here when published.</p></div>}
    </section>

    <aside class="knowledge-people shell" aria-labelledby="people-title"><div><h2 id="people-title">People, with credit<br />where it belongs.</h2><p>Each published piece names its actual contributors.</p></div><ul>{Object.values(authorRegistry).map((person) => <li><a href={person.url}>{person.name}</a><span>View Lab contributions</span></li>)}</ul></aside>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
